    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "(OED s.v. horse n. 27c) | small bells used for decoration on a horse’s trappings (OED s.v. bell n.1 1a) | a bell to hang around the neck of a horse (OED s.v. horse n. IV 27c), jingle bells (quote) Whanne he rood men myghte his brydel heere Gynglen in a whistlynge wynd as cleere And eek as loude as dooth the chapel belle (MED s.v. ginglen, quote from Chaucer 1387-95) | a bell to hang around the neck of a horse (OED s.v. horse n. 27c), jingle bells (quote) Whanne he rood men myghte his brydel heere Gynglen in a whistlynge wynd as cleere And eek as loude as dooth the chapel belle (MED s.v. ginglen, quote from Chaucer 1387-95)" ;
